# ------------------------------------------------------------- chemical pot ---
# Widom insertion of a test water into the swollen membrane, to be compared with
# the same quantity in bulk water. The comparison is only meaningful if both
# sides use identical cutoff, kspace accuracy and water model -- see bulk.in.j2.
#
# The test particle is inserted but never kept, so this measures the free energy
# the *next* water would pay, which is exactly the saturation question.
molecule        h2o h2o.mol
Read molecule template h2o:
# Rigid water for Widom test insertions.
  1 molecules
  0 fragments
  0 bodies
  3 atoms with max type 10
  2 bonds with max type 9
  1 angles with max type 14
  0 dihedrals with max type 0
  0 impropers with max type 0
fix             w all widom 100 400 0 87234 300.0 mol h2o full_energy
WARNING: Molecule attributes do not match system attributes
For more information see https://docs.lammps.org/err0026 (src/molecule.cpp:3634)
variable        muex equal f_w[1]
variable        boltz equal f_w[2]
variable        wvol equal f_w[3]
# Preserve one observation per Widom burst.  Python groups this raw time series
# into contiguous blocks; averaging a whole block here leaves only n_blocks
# values and makes the effective-sample-size diagnostic impossible.
fix             muavg all ave/time 100 1 100 v_muex v_boltz v_wvol file mu.dat
run             50000
